# --- s048 Book I dd.14-15 q.2
n("n774","s048-01","per magistrum qui probat","la","source","Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 15, citing Augustine, *De Trin.* IV 20.28 (see n766): only a person that is from another is sent.","to-verify")
n("n775","s048-02","⟨honor⟩","la","textual","A prints *bonor*. In A's type at this resolution *h* and *b* are hard to tell apart, and B reads *honor*.","verified")
n("n776","s048-02","sapientia genita","la","source","*Sapientia genita*: the stock example of a ‘mixed’ term, essential (*sapientia*) qualified by a notional determinant (*genita*). Compare Augustine, *De Trin.* VII 1.2–2.3, on *sapientia de sapientia*.","to-verify")
n("n777","s048-02","opera trinitatis sunt indiuisa ad extra","la","source","The scholastic axiom *opera Trinitatis ad extra sunt indivisa*, regularly ascribed to Augustine; compare *De Trin.* I 4.7 (*inseparabiliter operentur*) and *Enchir.* 38.","to-verify")
n("n778","s048-02","⟨Quod⟩","la","textual","A prints Q with a superscript abbreviation (*Qꝫ*/*Qꝛ*). It is read *Quod*, which suits the syntax; *Que* is also possible. B is not legible at this point in the reproduction consulted.","uncertain")
n("n779","s048-03","vna est magistri","la","source","Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 15 c. 4 (*Quod Filius sit missus a se*), with Augustine, *De Trin.* II (as cited by Lombard), on the inseparable operation.","verified")
n("n780","s048-03","Ambrosius li. 2°. de spiritu sancto","la","source","Ambrose, quoted by Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 15 c. 4: *Cum non definitum fuerit per Prophetam a quo datus sit Filius, ostenditur datus gratia Trinitatis, ut etiam ipse Filius se dederit*. Gorris takes the book number from Lombard's preceding citation (*in II libro De Spiritu Sancto*). A later gloss on Lombard (LombardPress text cv8jk9) remarks that Lombard departs from Ambrose's meaning.","verified")
n("n781","s048-03","vt et iam filius ipse dederit se","la","textual","*et iam* (= *etiam*) is printed as two words in A.","certain")
n("n782","s048-04","Mitti est originari","la","source","The objection identifies temporal mission with origin. Compare Aquinas, *ST* I q. 43 a. 4, and Scotus, *Ord.* I dd. 14–16, on whether a person sends itself. The holder of this opinion is not named.","to-verify")
n("n783","s048-04","de incarnare et de incarnari","la","source","The whole Trinity *incarnates* (effects the incarnation) but only the Son is *incarnate*: a standard example that active and passive terms in God do not correspond one to one.","certain")
n("n784","s048-02","⟨honour⟩","en","translation","Following B's *honor*; A prints *bonor*.")

